From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] media: i2c: t715-sensor: the S5K4H5 and S5K6B2 as V4L2
 subdevices

libcamera's simple pipeline handler wants a media graph with the sensor
as a subdevice, but t715-camera.ko drove both sensors itself, behind a
single video node.

t715-sensor.ko is an I2C driver for the two sensors, each on its
bit-banged bus.  It owns their rails, reset (and the front's standby),
MCLK and pinctrl states, with the power sequences t715-camera.c used.
Its modes come from the firmware files <firmware-name>-m<N>.seq, written
verbatim; the size, the line and frame lengths and the pixel clock are
read back from the SMIA registers each table sets.  Controls: exposure,
analogue gain, both blankings, pixel rate, link frequency, test pattern,
flips and orientation, with the crop selections.  The rear DW9807 focus
motor is a lens subdevice tied to the sensor by an ancillary link, and
ramps as before.

The tables are Samsung's and are not in the tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
